A||||6||JohnnyK||Can I take the motors out of my headlights?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-25-2000||02:45 PM||||Well, finally happened, the left one just wouldn't go up. Which is odd, because it was working fine, and then all of a sudden it doesn't. I have to check if it is that gear. But anyways, can I manually raise them and then take the motor out, or does it need the motor in there to stay up? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||11-25-2000||02:50 PM||||Can you manually raise it? Probably. Yes it needs to motor to stay up. But you have to remove the entire assembly to get to motor out. Just pull it. Open the gear case. Clean all the junk out. turn the gear 180 and put it all back together with some good grease.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||11-25-2000||03:09 PM||||I think I found the problem. There is a long plastic lever-ish thing that connects to it, and looks like it is held onto by a clip. The clips not there, and the plastic piece wasn't connected. So I attached it, and it went up halfway? Could it be just cause there is no clip?||||reg||1
Z||000003||overlord||11-25-2000||08:23 PM||||ya that will do it......i had rebiult my headlight motor ssytem...got it all back together but noticed that little clip was broken..so   put it on anyways.......few weeks later , headlight wouldnt go up, clip was gone....replaced clip for 50 cents and alls well.||||reg||1
Z||000004||doughboySE||11-25-2000||08:38 PM||||just incase you ever have it happen again mine are up and have to stay up cause my left motor is gone as well.<BR>all you have to do is turn the knob in circles to raise the light it takes a bit but you will get there and once its up you have to unplug the plug that provides the power to the light or once you shut the lights off they will go down again. when unplugged the lights will stay up and just go on and off as you hit the switch.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-26-2000||08:22 AM||||If you have to remove the motors (to rebuild them), you can prop up the headlights with a can (bottle?) of oil.  Works great.  I personally know of one forum member who ran his car this way for um...way too long. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  BTW--If you have to do this, make sure you use a can of synthetic oil to prop the headlights up.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PlasticWrapd||11-27-2000||09:50 PM||||As a side note, The headlight motors from a 82-86 Firebird will fit the 84-86 Fiero.  The only difference is the left Firebird headlight motor fits the right Fiero Headlight.  Makes a HUGE difference in price if you ask for the Firebird part at the local salvage yard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
